On the reddest weekend of the season I visited an old hanok village. Sitting on the wooden porch, I could hear the wind slip round the eaves and drop into the courtyard.

## The light at four

As the sun lowers, the grain of the roof tiles sharpens and every maple leaf glows as if someone switched it on. Here are two more photos from that day.

![Clouds at dusk](media/dusk.jpg)
![A lake at dawn](media/lake.jpg)

### Getting there

1. Twenty minutes by village bus from the station
2. Ten minutes along the stone-wall lane
3. Pick up a map at the visitor centre

> Tip: go after three in the afternoon - fewer people, the best light.

---

Next time I want to photograph the same courtyard under snow.
